    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0516" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg404"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Northcott.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-10-28"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department has received your No. 12 of
                    the 1st instant inclosing copy and translation of a memorandum which the
                    Colombian minister for foreign affairs requested you to sign with him, proposing
                    that as it would be impossible to obtain the consent of the Colombian Congress
                    to the ratification of the United States-Panama-Colombia treaties, those
                    treaties be dropped and negotiations be opened at Bogota.</p>
                <p>The department commends your action in declining to sign the
                    memorandum-protocol.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
